WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.967
-Welcome, everybody.

00:00:01.967 --> 00:00:03.469
Welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:05.705
[ Cheers and applause ]
At home, if you're watching --

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:09.475
Look at you.
It is a -- It's a special night

00:00:09.475 --> 00:00:11.744
because, for the first time
since the pandemic,

00:00:11.744 --> 00:00:14.480
our audience is no longer
required to wear a mask.

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:16.182
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:19.452
♪♪

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:21.587
Smile!
Smile!

00:00:21.587 --> 00:00:23.523
You're on TV.

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:24.791
Yeah.

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:27.160
So, you better laugh
'cause I can see who isn't.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.295
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:30.763
What an exciting time this is.

00:00:30.763 --> 00:00:32.932
We're maskless,
fully vaccinated,

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:34.600
and it's officially summer.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:35.601
Official.
-Yeah.

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:37.770
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:39.905
It's great.

00:00:39.905 --> 00:00:42.241
That's right. Kids are pumped
that school is over

00:00:42.241 --> 00:00:44.811
while their parents are staring
blankly at a wall like,

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:47.680
"I thought we had more time."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.548
Yeah, and it's not just the
start of summer, you guys.

00:00:49.548 --> 00:00:52.318
It's also Amazon Prime Day.
-Hey!

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:54.387
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:56.522
That's right.
That's right.

00:00:56.522 --> 00:00:58.390
Today, instead of buying stuff
we don't need,

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:01.160
we buy stuff we don't need
at a slightly lower price.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:02.294
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.294 --> 00:01:03.563
I don't know what
an immersion blender is,

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:06.532
but, yeah, just look at
the price on that.

00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:07.767
How am I gonna make my coffee

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:09.068
if I don't have
an immersion blender?

00:01:09.068 --> 00:01:10.469
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.469 --> 00:01:13.172
Prime Day
is actually a two-day event.

00:01:13.172 --> 00:01:14.907
-Ooh.
-Yeah, Amazon is basically

00:01:14.907 --> 00:01:17.377
your annoying friend
who plans a birthday weekend.

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:20.847
[ Laughter ]
"You only get one day, Carl."

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:23.415
Yep, Amazon has deals
on outdoor cameras,

00:01:23.415 --> 00:01:27.420
digital recorders,
and night-vision binoculars.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.222
And with that much
spying capability,

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:32.124
you're basically Amazon.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.124 --> 00:01:34.727
You're at least Facebook.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:37.229
Some news from Washington.
This weekend, Kim Jong-un

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:40.233
made his first statement about
the Biden administration,

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:44.203
saying that he's prepared for
both dialogue and confrontation.

00:01:44.203 --> 00:01:46.306
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:47.940
That's right.
Kim Jong-un just challenged

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:51.578
Biden to a rap battle.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.578 --> 00:01:54.046
Yep, Kim Jong-un says that he's
prepared for both dialogue

00:01:54.046 --> 00:01:56.683
and confrontation.
It's the same thing my aunt says

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:58.718
when she walks into a T.J. Maxx.

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:00.720
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.289
"Let's go!"

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:05.391
Well, guys, the Olympics
are almost here, and today,

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:09.762
organizers announced that venues
will be at 50% capacity.

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:14.534
-Oh.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:17.136
-That's right. 50%,
which means only four people

00:02:17.136 --> 00:02:19.639
will be allowed to watch fencing
instead of the normal eight.

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:22.208
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:24.344
En garde!
-Chh!

00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:25.577
-Do they start
with the hand up here?

00:02:25.577 --> 00:02:28.248
-Sure. Why not?

00:02:28.248 --> 00:02:29.581
Yeah.
-Eventually -- I've seen this.

00:02:29.581 --> 00:02:31.284
-Eventually, it's épée.
-But does it start --

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:33.385
Like this, maybe?
-Yeah, maybe that.

00:02:33.385 --> 00:02:35.088
Maybe that.
That looks good.

00:02:35.088 --> 00:02:37.156
You look good like that.
-I look like a fencer there.

00:02:37.156 --> 00:02:38.624
-Yeah, a fencer
of stolen jewelry.

00:02:38.624 --> 00:02:41.127
-Just being cocky.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:42.629
-You got to put a pinky out
on the sword.

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:44.864
-Yeah, I throw the pinky out.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:46.132
-You know, class.
There you go.

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:47.466
-Class it up a little bit.
-Pure class.

00:02:47.466 --> 00:02:49.769
-Pinky out on the sword.
Like that?

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:51.670
Maybe like that?
-Yeah, like a flourish.

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:54.006
-Like a flour--
-Like jazz hands.

00:02:54.006 --> 00:02:55.140
Yeah, there you go.
There you go.

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:56.208
-This is how you fence?
-Yeah.

00:02:56.208 --> 00:02:57.810
♪♪

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.579
-That's how you fence?
-Yeah.

00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:01.446
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:01.446 --> 00:03:05.017
En garde!
Touché!

00:03:05.017 --> 00:03:08.587
-Also, they also said fans
aren't allowed to cheer.

00:03:08.587 --> 00:03:11.190
-Oh.
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:13.259
-Although they say that at the
beginning of every graduation,

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:15.961
and parents are still like,
"Thomas, yeah!

00:03:15.961 --> 00:03:17.930
Whoo!
Tommy, you did it!

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:21.301
That's my boy, Tommy!"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:24.037
Soccer superstar
Cristiano Ronaldo just became

00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:27.807
the first person in the world
to hit 300 million followers

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:28.941
on Instagram.
-Ooh.

00:03:28.941 --> 00:03:31.544
[ Cheers ]
-It's a pretty big deal.

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:32.945
and now a lot of people
are reaching out

00:03:32.945 --> 00:03:35.748
to congratulate him.
For example, Lionel Messi said,

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:37.817
"What an incredible achievement.
Way to go!"

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:39.018
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:40.653
Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson said,

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:42.021
"Congrats, pal,
but watch your back.

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:44.223
I'm coming for you."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.223 --> 00:03:46.092
Then Ronaldo himself
had this to say.

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:47.159
He said, "I can't believe it.

00:03:47.159 --> 00:03:48.894
Thank you so much
for the support."

00:03:48.894 --> 00:03:50.863
[ Laughter ]
It didn't stop there.

00:03:50.863 --> 00:03:53.499
Remember that statue of him?
-I knew it.

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:55.868
I knew it.
-Oh, no, it didn't --

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:58.837
-The bronze statue of Ronaldo
reached out and said...

00:03:58.837 --> 00:04:00.172
-Really?

00:04:00.172 --> 00:04:01.974
-"Ermagherd, yer nermber wern!"

00:04:01.974 --> 00:04:06.012
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.012 --> 00:04:09.048
-Oh, no.
-After that, Ariana Grande said,

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:11.584
"I hope I can get
to 300 million soon."

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:14.353
And the statue of Ronaldo
was like, "Mer ter!

00:04:14.353 --> 00:04:16.589
Er werna ber perpyerler!"

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:18.858
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:20.660
Wants to be "perpular."
-"Perpular"?

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:22.661
-Then this plaque
of Elvis Presley spoke up

00:04:22.661 --> 00:04:26.833
and said, "Yerr! Plers ferler
mer ern Ernstagrerm."

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:28.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:31.337
And finally this statue
of Lucille Ball said,

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:34.306
"Mer herndle ers
@rerl-lercerlle-berl.

00:04:34.306 --> 00:04:38.110
#Ferlerberk.
#Ernflererncer."

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:40.179
[ Cheers and applause ]
They're all very excited.

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:43.015
Good for him.
300 million is

00:04:43.015 --> 00:04:45.117
nothing to sneeze at.

00:04:45.117 --> 00:04:47.252
Listen to this.
I saw that NASA is struggling

00:04:47.252 --> 00:04:50.322
to fix a computer on
the Hubble Space Telescope

00:04:50.322 --> 00:04:53.692
that was developed in the 1980s.
Yeah.

00:04:53.692 --> 00:04:55.527
It's from the '80s,
so the manual only says,

00:04:55.527 --> 00:04:57.530
"Remove the circuit board
and blow on it."

00:04:57.530 --> 00:05:01.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:04.136
And finally, a grocery store in
Wisconsin is offering customers

00:05:04.136 --> 00:05:06.171
color-coded bracelets to show

00:05:06.171 --> 00:05:10.075
their social-distancing
comfort levels.

00:05:10.075 --> 00:05:13.479
Yeah, red means no contact.
Yellow means elbows only.

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:15.348
And green means open-mouth kiss.
-Oh.

00:05:15.348 --> 00:05:16.516
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.516 --> 00:05:19.085
As I mentioned,
today is Amazon Prime Day.

00:05:19.085 --> 00:05:20.886
People buy a ton of products
on Prime Day,

00:05:20.886 --> 00:05:22.321
but you can't always
trust the reviews.

00:05:22.321 --> 00:05:24.156
I just want
to remind everyone of that.

00:05:24.156 --> 00:05:27.159
I read that lately Amazon had to
crack down on the fake ones.

00:05:27.159 --> 00:05:30.229
Luckily, you can usually tell
when a review is fake, though.

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:33.065
For example,
here's a bed tray table.

00:05:33.065 --> 00:05:34.566
Here's a fake review that says,

00:05:34.566 --> 00:05:36.936
"I love this
for breakfast in bed."

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:38.604
The real review says,
"I love feeling like

00:05:38.604 --> 00:05:41.240
my bedroom's in a hospital."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:42.641
-That's the real review?

00:05:42.641 --> 00:05:45.845
-Yeah, like here's a pack of
anti-chafing nipple guards.

00:05:45.845 --> 00:05:47.480
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:50.849
The fake review says, "Provides
great protection on long runs."

00:05:50.849 --> 00:05:52.718
The real review says,
"Ripping these off

00:05:52.718 --> 00:05:54.219
is the male equivalent
of childbirth."

00:05:54.219 --> 00:05:58.257
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:58.257 --> 00:06:01.827
Next is a Teton Sports
hiking backpack.

00:06:01.827 --> 00:06:04.163
Fake review says,
"A rugged backpack

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:05.998
that's perfect
for overnight hikes."

00:06:05.998 --> 00:06:08.100
The real review says,
"It'll sit in your closet

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:10.436
for three years
with a half eaten Clif bar

00:06:10.436 --> 00:06:13.939
in the front pocket."
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:13.939 --> 00:06:17.309
-That's where I left
that Clif bar.

00:06:17.309 --> 00:06:19.979
Next up, here's an
Astro gaming headset.

00:06:19.979 --> 00:06:21.848
The fake review says,
"Amazing sound.

00:06:21.848 --> 00:06:24.549
Took my online gaming
to the next level."

00:06:24.549 --> 00:06:27.019
But the real review says,
"Plays so loud, I didn't hear

00:06:27.019 --> 00:06:28.588
my girlfriend say,
I'm leaving you, Kevin."

00:06:28.588 --> 00:06:31.624
[ Laughter ]

00:06:31.624 --> 00:06:33.992
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:33.992 --> 00:06:37.763
"He's hiding, he's hiding,
he's hiding!"

00:06:37.763 --> 00:06:40.833
Finally, here's a waterproof
phone pouch.

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:43.369
Fake review says,
"Kept my phone safe and dry

00:06:43.369 --> 00:06:44.770
while I went in the water."

00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:47.173
Real review says, "My phone
is at the bottom of a lake,

00:06:47.173 --> 00:06:48.574
but at least
it's still working."

00:06:48.574 --> 00:06:50.576
[ Laughter ]
There you go, everybody.

